  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Intra-Regional Labour Migration for Local Development in West African Countries - Migration for Development Program (MDP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Countries in West Africa (WA) have historically been involved in frequent movements within the region. Cross-border movements are considered a key element for improving livelihood strategies, as well as an adaptation strategy in the face of the recent health, socio-economic and climatic stressors. The COVID-19 pandemic has severely affected mobility through numerous direct and indirect pathways, including the socio-economic crisis that is expected to produce massive unemployment in WA, affecting sustainable development. Border and rural areas of Senegal, The Gambia, Guinea-Bissau, and Guinea, are among the most affected by this crisis. IOM proposes to enhance the socio-economic development and intra-regional mobility of the four countries&#x2019; rural areas through youth-driven programs.</narrative>
  </description>
